2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:48:20-07:00","id":867215,"title":"","content":"As a Detroit resident and a petrol head, I am so incredibly totally psyched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:51:56-07:00","id":867219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867197#post867197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The classic 'you scratched my car' or 'guy knocks over a bunch of motorcycles,' scenes get a lot more violent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scratching a lodge member's car!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That is obviously sound justification for a immediate Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> A polite apology and exchanging insurance information will not save such pitiful fools.<br /> <br /> These guys are source of nightmares for parking attendants and valets across the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:56:01-07:00","id":867225,"title":"","content":"<b><i>YES!!!</i></b><br /> <br /> Now, I can start converting some Lodges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:06:47-07:00","id":867233,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note, I admit to having a little difficulty imagining these guys within a mixed pack.<br /> <br /> Are the Steel Teeth supposed to only exist in packs exclusively of lodge members?<br /> <br /> Their traveling and priorities, particularly their harsh ban, certainly make life among a typical, geographical territorial pack exceedingly difficult.<br /> <br /> Is the Sacred Hunt benefits of the Steel Teeth a Siskur-Dah Condition like the regular tribes?<br /> <br /> If a Steel Teeth Lodge member is a Ritemaster of a Sikur-Dah for a mixed pack, do all participating werewolves also gain the Steel Teeth Sacred Hunt benefits?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:15:06-07:00","id":867243,"title":"","content":"I couldn't speak for the rules, but the ban really isn't that difficult, my character is basically under it as it is and it doesn't interfere with his interactions with the rest of the pack. We don't all sleep in the same place. It's a little like Promethean, but obviously not as harsh.<br /> <br /> A game with a limited focus on a small town or wilderness area, and obviously Neolithic era games aren't going to have much room for it. But if you were in a larger city or part of a traveling game members would be vital. Our last werewolf game ended up with a massive road trip across the Northeast, the Atlantic, then Europe to Russia, while another game took place entirely within the confines of a tropical island that had one unfinished road that stretched for half a mile. Obviously a group and their storyteller should talk about it beforehand to see if it's appropriate and if plots can be built to take advantage of the lodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:17:04-07:00","id":867244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867233#post867233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the Sacred Hunt benefits of the Steel Teeth a Siskur-Dah Condition like the regular tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Steel Teeth Lodge member is a Ritemaster of a Sikur-Dah for a mixed pack, do all participating werewolves also gain the Steel Teeth Sacred Hunt benefits?<br /> </div> </div> </div> \u200bYep!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:24:09-07:00","id":867247,"title":"","content":"Can members grant this benefit <i>instead of</i> or <i>in addition to</i> any benefit they would normally give through the Rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:26:33-07:00","id":867250,"title":"","content":"Instead of. Lodges give additional specialised tools for the sacred hunt toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:28:11-07:00","id":867252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867243#post867243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't speak for the rules, but the ban really isn't that difficult, my character is basically under it as it is and it doesn't interfere with his interactions with the rest of the pack. We don't all sleep in the same place. It's a little like Promethean, but obviously not as harsh.<br /> <br /> A game with a limited focus on a small town or wilderness area, and obviously Neolithic era games aren't going to have much room for it. But if you were in a larger city or part of a traveling game members would be vital. Our last werewolf game ended up with a massive road trip across the Northeast, the Atlantic, then Europe to Russia, while another game took place entirely within the confines of a tropical island that had one unfinished road that stretched for half a mile. Obviously a group and their storyteller should talk about it beforehand to see if it's appropriate and if plots can be built to take advantage of the lodge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I certainly don't believe Steel Teeth wouldn't be <i>useful</i>.<br /> <br /> However, a werewolf effectively compelled to travel constantly and hunt across territories is certainly challenging for a splat largely designed around holding and protecting discrete geographic territory.<br /> <br /> The Steel Teeth are definitely neat and fun, but absent a <i>lot</i> of player and ST agreement and planning, I also envision serious potential problems if they're part of a mixed group<br /> <br /> I'm also actually more interested in the rules and mechanics, as I surmise they will be applicable to all lodges.<br /> <br /> For instance, if the additional Sacred Hunt lodge benefits can be shared with your pack like a regular Siskur-Dah Condition, the motivation for pack members to join lodges substantially increases.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Ninj'd. Chris answered the rules questions while I was typing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:33:57-07:00","id":867255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867250#post867250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of. Lodges give additional specialised tools for the sacred hunt toolbox.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for example, a Iron Master Steel Teeth ritemaster can choose whether to grant the Iron Master <i>OR</i> Steel Teeth Siskur-Dah Condition to his pack?<br /> <br /> Lodge Sacred Hunt benefits supplement, not replace, tribe Siskur-Dah Conditions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:38:02-07:00","id":867259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867255#post867255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, for example, a Iron Master Steel Teeth ritemaster can choose whether to grant the Iron Master <i>OR</i> Steel Teeth Siskur-Dah Condition to his pack?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThat's correct. A lodge-member ritemaster invoking the Sacred Hunt can bestow either their tribe Siskur-Dah or their lodge one; they basically now have a choice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:39:57-07:00","id":867261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867252#post867252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, a werewolf effectively compelled to travel constantly and hunt across territories is certainly challenging for a splat largely designed around holding and protecting discrete geographic territory.<br /> <br /> The Steel Teeth are definitely neat and fun, but absent a <i>lot</i> of player and ST agreement and planning, I also envision serious potential problems if they're part of a mixed group</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're under some misconceptions. It doesn't say they are compelled to travel constantly, only that those in less densely settled territories tend to be nomadic. And hunting across territories is something every werewolf is likely to deal with, as the sacred hunt doesn't stop at some line in the sand. I wouldn't even go so far as to say that the splat is designed around protecting a discrete geographic territory, that's certainly a standard way to do it but some packs are going to have very abstract methods of hunting, a pack in the form of a company is going to go wherever their business is, a biker gang wherever their bikes go, Ivory Claws wherever their blood is. One of the first lodges mentioned in the game are called out for being nomads who travel to get the stories of fallen werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:46:06-07:00","id":867267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867259#post867259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's correct. A lodge-member ritemaster invoking the Sacred Hunt can bestow either their tribe Siskur-Dah or their lodge one; they basically now have a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Absent a <i>really</i> crappy Ban or Totem, there's really no reason not to join a Lodge. They offer significant personal benefits, pack advantages, and interesting thematic hooks.<br /> <br /> Does joining a Lodge and acquiring its benefits cost XP and/or require attribute and skill prerequisites, similar to the new Mage 2e Legacy rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T18:51:36-07:00","id":867272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867267#post867267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does joining a Lodge and acquiring its benefits cost XP and/or require attribute and skill prerequisites, similar to the new Mage 2e Legacy rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere's no cost in experiences and no hard mechanical set of skill or attribute prerequisites. The first half of the Lodges section in The Pack covers things like how lodges apply standards, requirements, trials and the like for potential adherents, but these aren't linked to particular numbers of dots or the like. It depends a lot on the supplicant, the lodge members dealing with the supplicant and, most importantly of all, the totem.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:28:47-07:00","id":867293,"title":"","content":"I love how cultic and strangely intimate Lodges are now. Tribes feel like these enormous, ideological connections that are as tight-knit as the local community decides that they are, much like groups of larger religions. Lodges are entirely different, very individualized, and extremely personal. I absolutely love it, but I'm not sure I'm the best person to describe exactly why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T01:51:47-07:00","id":867441,"title":"","content":"A Steel Tooth staying in one place just needs two places to sleep, a mile apart - that's a meaningful restriction that puts limits on you that can be exploited if you're being hunted, but it doesn't totally screw you; a werewolf shouldn't have much trouble <i>running</i> a mile to get to their other sleeping spot, if they need to... as long as they're not interrupted.<br /> <br /> I like the Ban - it puts a meaningful but not crippling restriction on you if you're sticking around one place, but if you're acting like the archetypal nomadic Steel Tooth it disappears into things you're doing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:50:04-07:00","id":867513,"title":"","content":"A mile apart isn't that big of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:15:43-07:00","id":867767,"title":"","content":"A Knights of St. Adrian teamup...<br /> <br /> Or fight.<br /> <br /> Either would be epic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T19:34:13-07:00","id":868073,"title":"","content":"Awesome, indeed. I'm very excited for the book!<br /> <br /> On the Ban: My girlfriend lives 5 miles away from me, and we usually take turns on which homes we sleep. Not that hard at all in normal circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T05:17:00-07:00","id":868330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=867293#post867293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love how cultic and strangely intimate Lodges are now. Tribes feel like these enormous, ideological connections that are as tight-knit as the local community decides that they are, much like groups of larger religions. Lodges are entirely different, very individualized, and extremely personal. I absolutely love it, but I'm not sure I'm the best person to describe exactly why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. It's like saying, &quot;Oh, yeah I'm Christian&quot; to another one on the other side of the world: very broad and open ended while still providing a common discourse...and then saying, &quot;Oh, but this is my <i>church</i> where we fucking go <i>metal</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T10:18:50-07:00","id":868536,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/3I2RgdV.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm really enjoying the Thousand Steel Teeth more and more. It's a nice inversion that really fits with car culture. They're actively helping the prey. Smoke Drinker is a predator, like all spirits, but it doesn't seem to be a hunter. Instead it's the hunted. And a hunted that looks like it makes a huge mess in the Hisil when it comes around.<br /> <br /> The Lodge Aspiration is super cool, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T07:46:32-07:00","id":869309,"title":"","content":"What I want to know is this: how does Smoke Drinker cross the ocean? Is the lodge ban usually the same as the totem's ban?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:44:26-07:00","id":869345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=869309#post869309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to know is this: how does Smoke Drinker cross the ocean? Is the lodge ban usually the same as the totem's ban?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A totem\u2019s ban is appropriate for its Rank, as described on p. 185. Pack members must uphold the totem\u2019s ban; a pack member who disregards the totem\u2019s ban once will suffer it as a Ban Condition. If she breaches the ban again, she loses her dots in the Totem Merit. </div> </div> </div>That's just for packs, but it might be the same ban. I'm not sure if the tribal bans are the same.<br /> <br /> For crossing the ocean, perhaps it moves so fast it can go over water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T08:54:22-07:00","id":869357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=869309#post869309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I want to know is this: how does Smoke Drinker cross the ocean?</div> </div> </div> </div>A question that probably has interesting answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b Is the lodge ban usually the same as the totem's ban? </div> </div> </div> Lodge bans generally reflect the totem's ban but are not necessarily exactly the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T09:41:03-07:00","id":869386,"title":"","content":"I imagine Smoke-Drinker's ban likely has to do with improving itself; at least, it fits with the sacrifices of cars and its fear of becoming obsolete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:05:41-07:00","id":869402,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't make much sense for a spirit to have a ban about where they can sleep, seeing as they generally don't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:09:38-07:00","id":869405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=869402#post869402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wouldn't make much sense for a spirit to have a ban about where they can sleep, seeing as they generally don't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. If it is within the concept of the spirit, they will. Take Black Wolf guarding her siblings dens while they slept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:21:41-07:00","id":869411,"title":"","content":"Weren't the firstborn originally Pangaeans? That might have made them work differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T10:38:58-07:00","id":869420,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the daytime cycle of Helios put a lot of spirits to dormancy? That could be a spiritual equivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T14:59:58-07:00","id":869690,"title":"","content":"If the decision was up to me, the Smoke Drinker itself would have a brutally direct &quot;never stop moving.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not plausible for werewolves - they <i>do</i> need to sleep - so they get something thematically related that's more realistic for beings partly of the Flesh to maintain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T15:58:35-07:00","id":869728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=869411#post869411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the firstborn originally Pangaeans? That might have made them work differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind the fact there's fetishes alluding to spirits dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:43:58-07:00","id":870337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=869690#post869690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the decision was up to me, the Smoke Drinker itself would have a brutally direct &quot;never stop moving.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's not plausible for werewolves - they <i>do</i> need to sleep - so they get something thematically related that's more realistic for beings partly of the Flesh to maintain.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always maintained that Spirit Totems impose Bans that feed them Essence, instead of Bans that are similar to theirs. An Arson Spirit will require his followers to burn something of value once a month, while Smoke Drinker requires his followers to never sleep at the same place twice, probably because the act of moving away gives him Essence to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:18:50-07:00","id":870445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=870337#post870337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always maintained that Spirit Totems impose Bans that feed them Essence, instead of Bans that are similar to theirs. An Arson Spirit will require his followers to burn something of value once a month, while Smoke Drinker requires his followers to never sleep at the same place twice, probably because the act of moving away gives him Essence to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plausible. I don't think the spirits <i>decide</i> what Ban to impose on a Lodge or Pack, though - I think it naturally emerges from their nature.<br /> <br /> At that point, the question gets very muddy; the same underlying thing (the nature of the spirit in question) informs its Ban, the Ban it gives to werewolves tied to it, and what it can feed on. It'd have to be a damn strange spirit for those three things to all inherit something completely different from its core nature.<br /> <br /> It's the nature of an Arson spirit to burn things, so it does that, feeds on other people doing that, and imposes that requirement on its werewolves; it's the nature of the Smoke Drinker to never stop moving, so it never stops moving, its werewolves never stop moving, and it feeds on that.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;can the spirit feed on this?&quot; is a good question to ask when inventing a Ban, but if I have a really strong idea that doesn't directly feed the spirit but does suit it in other ways I wouldn't worry about using it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:25:40-07:00","id":870458,"title":"","content":"I think fulfilling the Lodge or Totem Aspirations feeds the totem more than the Ban. The Ban brings you more in sync with the totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:34:27-07:00","id":870466,"title":"","content":"Actually, yeah, looking back at the corebook the example is a Fire spirit giving a Ban about being immersed in water. That's much less something that'll promote feeding than it could be.<br /> <br /> It's a cool way to help get inspiration, but I think nofather's right - the Aspiration is a better place for it, the carrot of &quot;do things I'd do&quot; to the Ban's stick of &quot;don't do anything I wouldn't.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:47:03-07:00","id":870481,"title":"","content":"Guess you both have very valid points. I'm still a bit tied to 1e and Aspirations didn't exist back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:47:52-07:00","id":871456,"title":"","content":"Can wolf blooded (the wolf blooded? wolf bloods?) join lodges? Which, if any, of the benefits do they gain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:08:03-07:00","id":871488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=871456#post871456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can wolf blooded (the wolf blooded? wolf bloods?) join lodges? Which, if any, of the benefits do they gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lodge of the Shield entry says this, 'Since the late \u201880s, the lodge\u2019s Wolf-Blooded membership has actually outnumbered its Uratha contingent, and the Lodge of the Shield is notable for the fact that Wolf-Blooded are permitted to hold positions outranking werewolf members.'<br /> <br /> And the Lodge of the Roman Ritual calls its Wolf-blooded members lay brethren. So it does look like they can join, but they're not always permitted to have high positions. I'm sure the benefits will be outlined in the Pack book, or afterward by the developer or writers. But it's not as if there's a ton of benefits granted that a wolf-blooded can take advantage of. The Aspiration and the Benefit seem likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:14:03-07:00","id":871498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=871456#post871456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can wolf blooded (the wolf blooded? wolf bloods?) join lodges? Which, if any, of the benefits do they gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDepends what you mean by join.<br /> <br /> Wolf-Blooded can be a part of a Lodge by dint of being socially accepted by werewolf Lodge members as part of it, but they gain none of the benefits, nor the ban, nor any actual spiritual bond to the Lodge at all. They can't access any merits that a Lodge might grant access to either (though they might *be* some of the benefits that a Lodge merit accesses - the Lodge of the Shield likely access to the Lodge Connections merit and plenty of those connections are likely Wolf-Blooded given the Lodge's structure)/ Werewolves are the <i>only </i>beings that can truly be Lodge members.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:19:13-07:00","id":871512,"title":"","content":"It's <i>possible</i> they might just answer your question ahead of time and I should be patient and stop blathering on and guessing, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:15:15-07:00","id":871590,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks for answering our questions Chris! I appreciate your answer too nofather, knowing that some of the write ups mention wolf-blooded members is useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:43:36-07:00","id":871620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solidork</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=871456#post871456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can wolf blooded (the wolf blooded? wolf bloods?) join lodges? Which, if any, of the benefits do they gain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would go &quot;Depends on the lodge&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:20:03-07:00","id":875843,"title":"","content":"This is a fascinating Lodge! For some reason it makes me think of Klaives from W:tA. With this Road Warrior feel, I would say that something like a Chain-Klaive would definitely work as a concept with this lodge. (Think WH40k chainswords, but made of silver.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T14:40:39-07:00","id":876002,"title":"","content":"I'm honestly somewhat inspired for a Mage Legacy (Matter-based, not sure what Path) of a similar cut for these guys to run with or against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:50:12-07:00","id":876528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/867031-get-your-motor-running-the-thousand-steel-teeth-werewolf-open-development?p=876002#post876002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm honestly somewhat inspired for a Mage Legacy (Matter-based, not sure what Path) of a similar cut for these guys to run with or against.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's probably something in there - you could actually go a long way with Lord of the Inanimate bikers, though there may well be some legs on going specifically vehicle-themed.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, nomadic travel/go-where-fate-takes-you themed Matter+Fate Acanthus legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}